    {
      "title": "Cedar Dimensions",
      "material": "Rigid polypropylene",
      "thickness": ".080\u2013.100 in., depending on profile",
      "profile": "Double 7 in. shingle; Double 9 in. hand-split shake; Triple 5 in. shingle; Half-Round",
      "height": "Profile-specific; select from the specification guide",
      "length": "Varies by shingle, shake and half-round profile",
      "body": [
        "Cedar Dimensions uses molded polypropylene panels to create the irregular edges and grain associated with cedar shingles and shakes. The family includes straight shingle, hand-split shake and half-round looks, so it can be used to change the character of a gable, porch or full wall rather than simply change its color.",
        "The profiles are separate panels with their own dimensions and matching corner pieces. Nominal thickness ranges from .080 to .100 inch across the family. A Double 7 shingle and a Double 9 shake should not be treated as interchangeable when calculating quantities or ordering trim.",
        "Choose the panel profile before the accessories. Ply Gem lists dedicated cedar-panel starter strips and profile-specific corners; those details give the wall a more convincing finish than using an unrelated lap-siding accessory. Color availability also varies by profile."
      ],
